From 53847c7b83789916f80da6dfc778a8ccef311afa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:24:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Cache audit: summary audit block, wrong-skip alert (ERROR
 line + ci_audit_alerts row), audit on runs and the overview

The engine (fenvix-engine-cli claude/audit-reruns) runs a seeded share of the skippable tests fresh and reports
audit {share, seed, checked, matched, wrong, flaky_evidence, wrong_tests} in summary.json. The App parses it, stores
the counts on ci_runs, writes one ci_audit_alerts row per wrong skip and logs it at ERROR; the check run and the PR
comment show it. Audited tests ran: never counted as skipped or billed as skipped. The dashboard shows this month's
audits per project and over all projects with the 95% upper bound, and the open alerts. Migration 0014 with its RLS
test (supabase/tests/audit-rls.sql).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YAF6Dfpa6pw8ofzmBuEkrk
