+**Skip audit (migration 0014).** In every run the engine runs a seeded random share of the tests it could skip
+(default 5%) and compares the fresh result with the cached one (outcome and test ids). Audited tests ran: they are in
+`tests.ran`, never in `tests.skippedWithProof`, so neither the dashboard nor the billing counts them as skipped.
+
+| Field | Type | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `audit` | `{ share, seed, checked, matched, wrong, flakyEvidence }` | `audit_*` columns of `ci_runs`, from `summary.json` → `audit`; `matched + wrong + flakyEvidence = checked ≤ tests.ran` |
+
+A **wrong skip** (two fresh runs contradicted the cached result) is one row of `ci_audit_alerts` (test id, cached and
+fresh outcomes, proof key, seed, `state` open or acknowledged) and an ERROR log line of the GitHub App
+(`alert: "cache_audit_wrong_skip"`). The overview shows this month's audits over all projects and per project with the
+one-sided 95% upper bound on the wrong-skip rate (3 / checked when none is wrong, else Clopper-Pearson), and the open
+alerts.
+
